.TH SRV 4
.SH NAME
srv \- dial a service and post the connection in /srv
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B srv
.I addr name
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Srv
dials
.IR addr ,
a dial string such as
.BR tcp!fs!9fs ,
and posts the stream as
.BI /srv/ name.
A mount of that name then makes the kernel a 9P client of whatever answers
the far end, the way it is of a posted pipe:
.IP
.EX
% srv tcp!fs!9fs fs
% mount /srv/fs /n/fs
.EE
.PP
The rc function
.B 9fs
in
.B /lib/rcmain
is the two lines as one:
.B 9fs fs
mounts the machine
.B fs
at
.BR /n/fs .
The conversation outlives
.IR srv :
the posting holds it, and removing the name is what ends it.
.SH SOURCE
.B cmd/srv/main.odin
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR import (4),
.IR exportfs (4),
.IR bind (1)
.SH BUGS
There is no authentication yet.
